<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vel' d'Hiv Roundup</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16–17 July <a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Rafle du Vel' d'Hiv</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vel' d'Hiv Roundup was a mass arrest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> on 16–17 July 1942, carried out by French police under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> government at German request. About 13,000 people, including some 4,000 children, were seized; many were held in the Vélodrome d'Hiver cycling stadium before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiecim">Auschwitz</a>, and very few survived. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> officially acknowledged its responsibility in 1995.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vel-dhiv-roundup.jpg" alt="Vel' d'Hiv Roundup" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Djampa · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rafle_du_Vel_d%27Hiv_plaque.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
